      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sophie emanates a fragility that extends beyond her physical form. Her cries, a blend of raw innocence and a desperate yearning for reassurance, prompt the medical staff to come closer, their protective instincts triggered by her vulnerability. They shift towards her slowly, their touch gentle—hands offering comfort rather than the usual clinical efficiency.\n\nIn contrast, Andre's arrival disrupts the thin veil of routine that surrounds the trauma bay with a palpable tension. His formidable presence in the form of tightly clenched fists, relentless gaze, and minimal verbal interaction speaks volumes of a man unready for the unfamiliar calm of medical examination. When he coughs or shifts in his chair, the medical team heightens their vigilance, his unpredictable nature manifesting in cautious glances and nervous glides of their fingers as they test his vitals. A new kind of distance is present, a blend of professional necessity and primal instinct to shield themselves from his volatile energy. As Andre’s gaze lands on them, their stoic faces relax just enough to offer a palliative attempt at conversation—calm, measured words that seek to assure him they are there to help, yet ever watching.",
